# Force LF everywhere, regardless of a given machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# sarran-ai/scripts/stamp.py content-hashes styles.css and main.js into their
# own filenames, and every page references that exact hash. Without this
# file, core.autocrlf=true (the common Windows default - it's what this repo
# was cloned under) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes those
# files' bytes and therefore their SHA256 - so the same commit can produce a
# different "correct" hash on every machine, or even on a second checkout on
# the same machine. `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes every text file to LF both
# in the repository and on checkout, on every platform, so the hash stays
# identical everywhere the repo is cloned.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these - they are binary and must round-trip byte-for-byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
